look material
# LockMaterial. Password "mock" (Rust only; QML leaves via ipc lock unlock).
# Step 1: light reveal
wait 1
rec reveal 1.5 ipc lock lock
note FAILED earlier: Rust showed black frames with the clock already faded in, then the wallpaper circle within ~3 frames (50-100 ms, no visible opening); QML opens the circle (with the clock inside) from the centre over ~0.7 s. PASS needs: black with a circle opening from the centre over ~450 ms (emphasized), the clock thickening from thin.
wait 1
# Step 2: pill
shot pill-closed
note Pill closed: avatar cookie + name only.
ptr move 900 400 sleep 300 glide 900 500 300 sleep 700
shot pill-open
note Pointer glide opens the pill to 360 px (spring) with placeholder "Enter password" (PASS earlier; spring width not measured, compare opening with QML).
wait 11
shot pill-closed-again
note About 10 s idle later the pill is closed again (PASS earlier).
key x
wait 0.5
shot pill-typed
note A key opens the pill with one dot.
key -k BackSpace
wait 11
shot pill-closed-3
note Closed again about 10 s after the backspace.
ptr move 960 700 sleep 200 click down up
# NOTE: click on layer surfaces may not register in the harness (it worked once earlier)
wait 1
shot pill-click
note A click on the closed pill opens it.
# Step 3: wrong password
key nope
wait 0.3
rec wrong 2 key -k Return
note Spinner in the send slot, avatar turns 40 degrees, then an error pill above the pill ("Incorrect password. Try again."), pill border red, the pill shakes (decaying spring ~0.7 s), pill stays open (text/pill PASS earlier; avatar turn and shake NOT inspected).
wait 1.5
# Step 5: fingerprint
ipc lock demo finger
wait 0.8
shot finger
note Target circle (secondaryContainer) beside the arrow pulses, round target springs from 1.15 (PASS earlier).
ipc lock demo miss
wait 0.5
shot miss
note errorContainer circle, shake, line "Not recognised. Try again" (PASS earlier).
ipc lock demo match
wait 0.4
shot match
note Cookie + check + ripple ring growing to 280 px over 600 ms (ring timing NOT measured earlier).
ipc lock demo off
# Step 6: face
ipc lock demo face
wait 0.8
shot face
note NOT RUN earlier: the lock icon at the top becomes the loading indicator; line "Looking for your face..." with the smiley.
ipc lock demo off
# Step 7: clock faces
# MANUAL: for lock.clockFace in stacked, dynamic, wide, overlap, analog, weather: lock + shot. FAILED earlier: in overlap and weather Rust draws the date line ("Saturday 7 November") UNDER/behind the notification shelf and clipped; QML keeps the date above the shelf. Stacked, dynamic (24h "7 Nov", 12h "PM"), wide, analog (hands at the time) were fine.
# MANUAL: lock.clockSize "small": the clock springs into the top-left (record; compare duration with QML; cross-over animation not captured earlier)
shot clock-default
note Default clock face as QML (stacked: thin big clock, date line above the notification shelf, nothing overlapping). Check the date line is NOT drawn under the shelf.
# Step 8: Now Playing
# MANUAL: with a player with a length: card above the pill; timeline visible within 1 s and wavy, moving while playing; pause: button rounds, timeline flat; position advances each second (NOT RUN earlier)
# Step 9: notifications
setup notify-send -a Firefox -i firefox 'Download finished' 'report.pdf'
setup notify-send -a Files -i org.gnome.Nautilus 'Copied' '3 files'
wait 1.5
shot notes
note Material shapes: shelf as a 52 px pill, cards 72 px (shelf shows, PASS partly earlier; sizes not measured). Icons real Colloid icons.
# Step 10: minute tick
# NOTE: needs a minute change; the runner may need to start this near :59
wait 1
ipc lock demo off
ipc lock unlock
wait 2
